      equipment: 'Poker chips, standard deck.',
      dealing: 'Each player antes. Dealer deals five cards face down to each player. All players simultaneously expose one card (roll). Highest card holder selects a partner; then the highest unpartnered player selects a partner, and so on until all are paired. Each partnership combines their eight remaining cards and selects three to use with their two upcards to form a five-card hand. Three betting rounds follow, with one of the three chosen cards turned face up after each round.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'After ante and deal, all players roll one card simultaneously. Partner selection proceeds by rank of the exposed card: highest picks first, then highest unpartnered, until all are paired. Each partnership combines their eight remaining cards and selects three to use with their two upcards to form a five-card hand. There are three betting rounds; after each round one of the three chosen cards is turned face up. Partners play as a team but bet as individuals: if one folds the other may continue. At showdown the team with the highest hand shares the pot; if one partner folded, the other wins the whole pot.',
