    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Win the pot by having the best five-card poker hand at showdown as a partnership, or by being the last partnership with a member still in the hand. If one member of the winning partnership folded, the remaining partner wins the whole pot.',
      'Turn-flow example: After ante and deal, all players roll one card simultaneously. Partner selection proceeds by rank of the exposed card: highest picks first, then highest unpartnered, until all are paired. Each partnership combines their eight remaining cards and selects three to use with their two upcards to form a five-card hand. There are three betting rounds; after each round one of the three chosen cards is turned face up. Partners play as a team but bet as individuals: if one folds the other may continue. At showdown the team with the highest hand shares the pot; if one partner folded, the other wins the whole pot.',
      'Scoring example: Points or match rules. Partnership with the best five-card poker hand at showdown wins and shares the pot; if one member of the winning partnership folded, the remaining partner wins the whole pot..',
